{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.WeightedCountConvolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.WeightedCountConvolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WeightedCountConvolution.weighted_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WeightedCountConvolution.weighted_pow","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WeightedCountConvolution.lean#L50-L56","doc":"Consequently the weighted count of a juxtaposition of `m` copies is the `m`-th power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WeightedCountConvolution.weighted_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WeightedCountConvolution.weighted_mul","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WeightedCountConvolution.lean#L42-L48","doc":"Disjoint juxtaposition multiplies the weighted counts: convolution of the `N_k` is\npolynomial multiplication, and the weight `x^{n}` is additive in `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WeightedCountConvolution.weighted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WeightedCountConvolution.weighted","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WeightedCountConvolution.lean#L39-L40","doc":"`Σ_k a_k x^{n−2k}`, written as `x^n · P(x⁻²)` for `P = Σ a_k Y^k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}